  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "The link's waver, debris paths, burst sparks, glyph angle and crack pattern vary per cast. The focus length, the seize moment and the crush moment stay fixed: the crush is the hit frame and the lift is the window to break free."
  },
  "director_notes": "An original telekinetic attack. Psychic force is mostly invisible, so the spell is told through what it does to space and to the target rather than through a projectile. Choices: (1) warped space is the main language: refraction ripples drawn as soft camera-facing rings (ring plane billboard) pulse out from the hand, close in around the target and spring back out after the crush; in an engine they should be screen-space distortion with only a faint pink edge; (2) the target is held in a bubble of force (orb with height_px so it surrounds the body, strong fresnel rim) with a glyph turning under it and debris floating up, then crushed by keyframing the bubble from 64 px to 10 px in 0.18 s while a ripple is sucked in; (3) a thin wavering link with two twisting strands joins caster and target, so it reads as one caster's grip from every view. Pink with a violet secondary and a cyan accent keeps it apart from arcane purple. The viewer cannot lift the target stand-in; the lift is in the beat intents and the debris, and a game should raise the target about half a body height during lift and drop it on the crush. Sound: shimmer while focusing, a light whoosh on the seize, a high hum while held, crash plus a low impact on the crush, a quiet shimmer tail."
}
